`GIVEN NOTICE` MEANS `I was given notice of the decision`
`NOTICE NOT GIVEN` MEANS `notice of the decision had to be given to me but was not`
`NO NOTICE NEEDED` MEANS `no notice had to be given to me, and none was`
`S12 DECISION` MEANS `the decision is taken to have been made under s 12 (nothing was done within the period)`

`APPLIED IN TIME` MEANS `in time: you applied on or before the last day s 10 allows`
`STILL IN TIME` MEANS `still in time: you have not applied, and the last day s 10 allows has not passed`
`APPLIED LATE` MEANS `out of time under s 10 (the text's no): the application for review was not made within the period`

`contract` MEANS `a claim about a contract, including damages for breach of contract`
`negligence` MEANS `a claim for damages for negligence or another tort, other than nuisance or trespass to land`
`debt` MEANS `a claim to recover a debt`
`goods` MEANS `a claim about goods or services supplied, including damages for detaining goods or for their return`
`debt declaration` MEANS `a claim for a declaration that I am, or am not, indebted to the other party (or for a stated amount)`
`common boundaries` MEANS `a claim for a determination under the Common Boundaries Act 1981 (or a variation of one)`
`fair work` MEANS `a fair work claim (under the Magistrates Court Act 1930 s 266E)`
`other claim` MEANS `something else`

`NOT CIVIL` MEANS `not a civil dispute application, so Part 4 and its limit do not apply (the text's no)`
`NO LIMIT` MEANS `yes: the $25 000 limit does not apply to this application (s 18 (3))`
`WITHIN LIMIT` MEANS `yes: the amount counted is not more than $25 000 (s 18 (2))`
`BY AGREEMENT` MEANS `yes, the whole amount: the parties agree to ACAT deciding it and the tribunal is satisfied they understand the excess over $25 000 is not abandoned (s 21)`
`ABANDON EXCESS` MEANS `yes, but only for $25 000: you abandon the excess by limiting your claim to $25 000, and the excess cannot be recovered (s 20)`
`OVER LIMIT` MEANS `no: the amount counted is more than $25 000 and neither s 20 nor s 21 allows it (the text's no, s 18 (1))`

`S22B NOT APPLY` MEANS `s 22B does not apply: the decision is not one you may apply to ACAT to review, or you did not ask in writing within the time allowed (the text's no: its "if" fails)`
`IN THE DECISION` MEANS `no reasons statement is required: the decision itself contains what a reasons statement would (s 22B (2) (a), the text's no)`
`ALREADY GIVEN` MEANS `no reasons statement is required: a document containing what a reasons statement would has already been given to you (s 22B (2) (b), the text's no)`
`CERTIFICATE` MEANS `not required in full: the Minister has certified that matter is not to be disclosed (s 22E); the decision-maker must tell you in writing within 28 days after the certificate what is left out and why (s 22E (3))`
`REASONS IN TIME` MEANS `given in time: within 28 days after the day you asked (s 22B (2))`
`REASONS NOT YET DUE` MEANS `not yet given, and the 28 days after the day you asked have not ended (s 22B (2))`
`REASONS LATE` MEANS `late: the 28 days after the day you asked have ended without the statement (s 22B (2) not complied with)`

`ASSISTANCE MAY` MEANS `the Minister may authorise legal or financial assistance by the Territory, on conditions the Minister sets; it is a discretion, not an entitlement (s 22T (3), (4))`
`ASSISTANCE NO` MEANS `no assistance on these facts: the Minister is not satisfied both that refusing would be a hardship to you and that granting it is reasonable (the text's no, s 22T (3))`
`ASSISTANCE APPLY` MEANS `you may apply to the Minister for assistance (s 22T (2)); you have not yet applied`
`ASSISTANCE NOT PART 4A` MEANS `s 22T does not apply: the matter is not one arising under Part 4A (review of a decision) (the text's no)`

`civil` MEANS `a civil dispute or another application`
`planning review` MEANS `a review of a decision under the Heritage Act 2004, the Planning Act 2023 or the Urban Forest Act 2023`
`FOI review` MEANS `a review under the Freedom of Information Act 2016 s 84 of a refusal to give access`
`FEES` MEANS `the filing fee, and any other fee the tribunal considers was necessary for the application (s 48 (2) (a))`
`DELAY COSTS` MEANS `the reasonable costs arising from the unreasonable delay or obstruction (s 48 (2) (b))`
`BREACH COSTS` MEANS `all or part of the costs of the application, on the Supreme Court scale, for contravening a tribunal order (s 48 (2) (c), s 49)`
`PLANNING COSTS` MEANS `the reasonable costs arising from a planning, heritage or urban forest review that was dismissed or struck out, including legal costs but not holding costs (s 48 (2) (d), (3))`
`FOI COSTS` MEANS `the reasonable costs arising from a freedom of information review in which access was ordered (s 48A)`

`DISMISSED` MEANS `your application may be dismissed (s 47A (2) (a))`
`DECIDED WITHOUT YOU` MEANS `the application may be decided without you (s 47A (2) (b))`
`REMOVED` MEANS `you may be removed as a party (s 47A (2) (c))`
`GOES ON` MEANS `the hearing may go on without you, be set down for another time, or other orders or steps may be ordered (s 47A (2) (d))`
`SET ASIDE` MEANS `you may apply to have an order made in your absence amended or set aside (s 56 (c) (i))`
`PAY TERRITORY` MEANS `you may be ordered to pay the Territory a stated amount, up to any amount a regulation prescribes (s 74 (2) (a))`
`STRUCK OUT` MEANS `your application may be struck out (s 74 (2) (b))`
`ORDER FOR APPLICANT` MEANS `an order may be made in favour of the applicant (s 74 (2) (c))`
`COSTS FOR BREACH` MEANS `you may be ordered to pay all or part of the other party's costs of the application, if the tribunal is satisfied it is in the interests of justice (s 48 (2) (c), s 49)`

`INTERIM MAY` MEANS `the tribunal may make any interim order it considers appropriate to protect your position; it lasts until the tribunal orders otherwise or the application is finalised (s 53 (2), (3))`
`INTERIM NO` MEANS `s 53 does not apply: the application has been finalised, you have not applied, or the tribunal is not satisfied you would be disadvantaged or harmed without it (the text's no: its "if" fails)`

`PAPERS NOTICE` MEANS `a notice that the tribunal proposes to decide my application on the documents, without a hearing (s 54 (2))`
`APPEAL DISMISSAL NOTICE` MEANS `a notice that the president proposes to dismiss my appeal as substantively similar to appeals already rejected (s 80 (1))`

`final order` MEANS `an order deciding the application, or another order that is not procedural`
`interim order` MEANS `an interim order under s 53`
`procedural order` MEANS `an order of a procedural nature (an adjournment, default judgment, or joining a party)`
`NO COPY RULE` MEANS `s 59 does not apply to an interim order under s 53 (the text's no)`
`REASONS YES` MEANS `yes: the tribunal must give you a written statement of reasons, or a transcript of its oral reasons (s 60 (2))`
`REASONS ASKED LATE` MEANS `no: you asked after the time allowed (the text's no: its "if" fails)`
`REASONS NOT FOR THIS ORDER` MEANS `no: s 60 does not apply to an interim order or an order of a procedural nature (the text's no, s 60 (4))`

`reviewable` MEANS `a decision ACAT can review`
`internally reviewable` MEANS `a decision that must or may be internally reviewed or reconsidered before ACAT review`
`not reviewable` MEANS `a decision ACAT cannot review`
`NOTICE 67A` MEANS `yes: the decision-maker must take reasonable steps to give you written notice (a reviewable decision notice, s 67A); a regulation may set its time and contents; if it is not given, the decision is still valid`
`NOTICE 67B` MEANS `yes: the decision-maker must take reasonable steps to give you written notice (an internal review notice, s 67B); a regulation may set its time and contents; if it is not given, the decision is still valid`
`NO NOTICE EXEMPT` MEANS `no: the decision does not impose a liability, penalty or limitation and does not adversely affect anyone else (the text's no, s 67A (2), s 67B (2))`
`NO NOTICE NOT AFFECTED` MEANS `no: your interests are not affected by the decision (the text's no)`
`NOTICE NOT ARISE` MEANS `ss 67A and 67B do not apply to a decision ACAT cannot review (NOTHING-kind)`

`money` MEANS `an order to pay money`
`non-money` MEANS `an order to do or not do something else`

`other kind` MEANS `any other application (a civil dispute, or a review under another law)`
`FOI` MEANS `a review of a decision under the Freedom of Information Act 2016`
`planning` MEANS `a heritage, planning or urban forest review (Heritage Act 2004, Planning Act 2023, Urban Forest Act 2023)`
`MAI` MEANS `an external review of an insurer's decision under the Motor Accident Injuries Act 2019, division 2.10.3`
`APPEAL YES` MEANS `yes: you may appeal to the appeal tribunal on a question of fact or law (s 79 (3)); the time for appealing is set by the tribunal's rules, not the Act`
`APPEAL EXCLUDED` MEANS `no appeal within ACAT for a freedom of information, heritage, planning or urban forest review (the text's no, s 79 (2)); see s 86 for the Supreme Court`
`APPEAL FROM APPEAL` MEANS `no appeal within ACAT from a decision that was itself on appeal (the text's no: its "if" fails); see s 86 for the Supreme Court`
`APPEAL NOT YET` MEANS `not yet: the tribunal has not decided the application (the text's no: its "if" fails)`
`APPEAL NOT PARTY` MEANS `s 79 gives the appeal to a party to the original application only (NOTHING-kind)`

`appeal tribunal` MEANS `a decision of the appeal tribunal`
`after s 80` MEANS `the original decision, after the president dismissed my appeal under s 80`
`after s 85` MEANS `the original decision, after the president decided not to deal with my appeal under s 85`
`original` MEANS `the original decision, without an appeal within ACAT`
`law` MEANS `a question of law`
`fact` MEANS `a question of fact only`
`SC FACT OR LAW` MEANS `yes, on a question of fact or law, but only with the Supreme Court's leave (s 86 (1), (4))`
`SC LAW` MEANS `yes, on a question of law, but only with the Supreme Court's leave (s 86 (2) or (3), (4))`
`SC LAW ONLY` MEANS `no: for this kind of application s 86 allows an appeal on a question of law only (the text's no)`
`SC NOT LISTED` MEANS `s 86 gives no appeal to the Supreme Court from that decision; appeal within ACAT first (s 79) (NOTHING-kind)`
`SC NOT PARTY` MEANS `s 86 gives the appeal to a party to the application only (NOTHING-kind)`

`REMOVE MUST` MEANS `yes: the parties applied jointly, so the tribunal must order removal (s 83 (1))`
`REMOVE MAY` MEANS `yes: you applied and the tribunal considers removal appropriate (s 83 (2))`
`REMOVE NO` MEANS `no: you applied alone and the tribunal does not consider removal appropriate (the text's no, s 83 (2))`
`REMOVE MAI` MEANS `no: s 83 does not apply to a motor accident injuries review or an appeal from one (the text's no, s 83 (3))`
`REMOVE NOT ARISE` MEANS `s 83 does not arise: no party has applied for removal (the text's no: its "if" fails)`

§ `The two regulative rules alone`

-- s 10: 28 days allowed; lodging on day 0, day 28 (the last day) is in time; day 29 is not.
#ASSERT `in time under` (`s 10 -- apply for review within the time allowed` 28) `the applicant` `lodge the application for review` 0
#ASSERT `in time under` (`s 10 -- apply for review within the time allowed` 28) `the applicant` `lodge the application for review` 28
#ASSERT NOT (`in time under` (`s 10 -- apply for review within the time allowed` 28) `the applicant` `lodge the application for review` 29)
-- s 22B: day 28 in time, day 29 not.
#ASSERT `in time under` `s 22B -- give the reasons statement within 28 days` `the decision-maker` `give the reasons statement` 28
#ASSERT NOT (`in time under` `s 22B -- give the reasons statement within 28 days` `the decision-maker` `give the reasons statement` 29)

§ `s 9, s 10 (1) -- a properly made application`

#ASSERT `s 10 (1) -- is my application properly made` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 10 (1) -- is my application properly made` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 10 (1) -- is my application properly made` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 10 (1) -- is my application properly made` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 10 (1) -- is my application properly made` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)

§ `s 12 -- deemed refusal`

-- Period ends 2 Mar 2026: on 3 Mar the decision-maker is taken to have refused; on 2 Mar (the last day) not yet.
#ASSERT `s 12 -- is the decision-maker taken to have refused` TRUE TRUE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` `3 Mar 2026`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 12 -- is the decision-maker taken to have refused` TRUE TRUE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` `2 Mar 2026`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 12 -- is the decision-maker taken to have refused` TRUE TRUE TRUE `2 Mar 2026` `3 Mar 2026`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 12 -- is the decision-maker taken to have refused` TRUE FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` `3 Mar 2026`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 12 -- is the decision-maker taken to have refused` FALSE TRUE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` `3 Mar 2026`)

§ `s 10 (2), (3), s 25 -- the last day to apply for review`

-- Decision 2 Mar 2026, notice given 7 Mar (5 days after: not "later than 5 days") -> 2 Mar + 28 = 30 Mar.
#ASSERT `s 10 -- the last day to apply for review` `2 Mar 2026` `GIVEN NOTICE` `7 Mar 2026` `2 Mar 2026` 0 FALSE EQUALS `30 Mar 2026`
-- Notice given 8 Mar (6 days after) -> 8 Mar + 28 = 5 Apr (s 10 (3) (a)).
#ASSERT `s 10 -- the last day to apply for review` `2 Mar 2026` `GIVEN NOTICE` `8 Mar 2026` `2 Mar 2026` 0 FALSE EQUALS `5 Apr 2026`
-- Notice required, not given; aware 20 Mar -> 17 Apr (s 10 (3) (b)).
#ASSERT `s 10 -- the last day to apply for review` `2 Mar 2026` `NOTICE NOT GIVEN` `2 Mar 2026` `20 Mar 2026` 0 FALSE EQUALS `17 Apr 2026`
-- No notice needed -> 30 Mar.
#ASSERT `s 10 -- the last day to apply for review` `2 Mar 2026` `NO NOTICE NEEDED` `20 Mar 2026` `20 Mar 2026` 0 FALSE EQUALS `30 Mar 2026`
-- Deemed decision under s 12, period ended 2 Mar -> 30 Mar (s 10 (3) (c)).
#ASSERT `s 10 -- the last day to apply for review` `2 Mar 2026` `S12 DECISION` `2 Mar 2026` `2 Mar 2026` 0 FALSE EQUALS `30 Mar 2026`
-- Rules allow 60 days -> 2 Mar + 60 = 1 May; barred by the authorising law -> 30 Mar; a shorter rule period is ignored.
#ASSERT `s 10 -- the last day to apply for review` `2 Mar 2026` `NO NOTICE NEEDED` `2 Mar 2026` `2 Mar 2026` 60 FALSE EQUALS `1 May 2026`
#ASSERT `s 10 -- the last day to apply for review` `2 Mar 2026` `NO NOTICE NEEDED` `2 Mar 2026` `2 Mar 2026` 60 TRUE EQUALS `30 Mar 2026`
#ASSERT `s 10 -- the last day to apply for review` `2 Mar 2026` `NO NOTICE NEEDED` `2 Mar 2026` `2 Mar 2026` 20 FALSE EQUALS `30 Mar 2026`

§ `s 10 -- am I in time to apply for review`

#ASSERT `s 10 -- am I in time to apply for review` `2 Mar 2026` `NO NOTICE NEEDED` `2 Mar 2026` `2 Mar 2026` 0 FALSE TRUE `30 Mar 2026` `1 Apr 2026` EQUALS `APPLIED IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 10 -- am I in time to apply for review` `2 Mar 2026` `NO NOTICE NEEDED` `2 Mar 2026` `2 Mar 2026` 0 FALSE TRUE `31 Mar 2026` `1 Apr 2026` EQUALS `APPLIED LATE`
#ASSERT `s 10 -- am I in time to apply for review` `2 Mar 2026` `NO NOTICE NEEDED` `2 Mar 2026` `2 Mar 2026` 0 FALSE TRUE `2 Mar 2026` `1 Apr 2026` EQUALS `APPLIED IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 10 -- am I in time to apply for review` `2 Mar 2026` `NO NOTICE NEEDED` `2 Mar 2026` `2 Mar 2026` 0 FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` `30 Mar 2026` EQUALS `STILL IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 10 -- am I in time to apply for review` `2 Mar 2026` `NO NOTICE NEEDED` `2 Mar 2026` `2 Mar 2026` 0 FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` `31 Mar 2026` EQUALS `APPLIED LATE`
-- Late notice (8 Mar): 5 Apr in time, 6 Apr late.
#ASSERT `s 10 -- am I in time to apply for review` `2 Mar 2026` `GIVEN NOTICE` `8 Mar 2026` `2 Mar 2026` 0 FALSE TRUE `5 Apr 2026` `6 Apr 2026` EQUALS `APPLIED IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 10 -- am I in time to apply for review` `2 Mar 2026` `GIVEN NOTICE` `8 Mar 2026` `2 Mar 2026` 0 FALSE TRUE `6 Apr 2026` `6 Apr 2026` EQUALS `APPLIED LATE`
-- Rules allow 60 days: 1 May in time, 2 May late.
#ASSERT `s 10 -- am I in time to apply for review` `2 Mar 2026` `NO NOTICE NEEDED` `2 Mar 2026` `2 Mar 2026` 60 FALSE TRUE `1 May 2026` `2 May 2026` EQUALS `APPLIED IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 10 -- am I in time to apply for review` `2 Mar 2026` `NO NOTICE NEEDED` `2 Mar 2026` `2 Mar 2026` 60 FALSE TRUE `2 May 2026` `2 May 2026` EQUALS `APPLIED LATE`

§ `s 16 -- civil dispute application`

#ASSERT `s 16 -- is my claim a civil dispute application` `negligence`
#ASSERT `s 16 -- is my claim a civil dispute application` `debt declaration`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 16 -- is my claim a civil dispute application` `fair work`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 16 -- is my claim a civil dispute application` `other claim`)

§ `ss 18-21 -- the $25 000 limit`

-- Exactly $25 000: within.
#ASSERT `ss 18-21 -- can ACAT hear my claim for this amount` `debt` 25000 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `WITHIN LIMIT`
-- $25 001, no way in: over the limit.
#ASSERT `ss 18-21 -- can ACAT hear my claim for this amount` `debt` 25001 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `OVER LIMIT`
-- $25 000.50 for a negligence claim: over.
#ASSERT `ss 18-21 -- can ACAT hear my claim for this amount` `negligence` 25000.5 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `OVER LIMIT`
-- $26 000 of which $1 500 interest: $24 500 counted (s 19 (1)).
#ASSERT `ss 18-21 -- can ACAT hear my claim for this amount` `debt` 26000 1500 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `WITHIN LIMIT`
-- Goods: value plus detention damages totalling $25 500, no interest: over.
#ASSERT `ss 18-21 -- can ACAT hear my claim for this amount` `goods` 25500 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `OVER LIMIT`
-- $30 000: abandon the excess when entitled in a court (s 20); not when not entitled.
#ASSERT `ss 18-21 -- can ACAT hear my claim for this amount` `contract` 30000 0 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `ABANDON EXCESS`
#ASSERT `ss 18-21 -- can ACAT hear my claim for this amount` `contract` 30000 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `OVER LIMIT`
-- By agreement (s 21): both conditions needed.
#ASSERT `ss 18-21 -- can ACAT hear my claim for this amount` `contract` 30000 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `BY AGREEMENT`
#ASSERT `ss 18-21 -- can ACAT hear my claim for this amount` `contract` 30000 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `OVER LIMIT`
-- Both s 20 and s 21 open: s 21 first (fork F6).
#ASSERT `ss 18-21 -- can ACAT hear my claim for this amount` `contract` 30000 0 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `BY AGREEMENT`
-- s 18 (3): common boundaries, or prescribed by regulation.
#ASSERT `ss 18-21 -- can ACAT hear my claim for this amount` `common boundaries` 100000 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NO LIMIT`
#ASSERT `ss 18-21 -- can ACAT hear my claim for this amount` `debt` 100000 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NO LIMIT`
-- Not a civil dispute application.
#ASSERT `ss 18-21 -- can ACAT hear my claim for this amount` `fair work` 1000 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOT CIVIL`

§ `s 82A -- removal of a combined fair work matter`

#ASSERT `s 82A -- must my application be removed to the Magistrates Court` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82A -- must my application be removed to the Magistrates Court` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82A -- must my application be removed to the Magistrates Court` FALSE TRUE TRUE)

§ `s 22B, s 22D -- reasons statements`

-- Decision 2 Mar 2026: ask by 30 Mar; rules allowing 42 days: 13 Apr.
#ASSERT `s 22B -- the last day to ask for a reasons statement` `2 Mar 2026` 0 EQUALS `30 Mar 2026`
#ASSERT `s 22B -- the last day to ask for a reasons statement` `2 Mar 2026` 42 EQUALS `13 Apr 2026`
-- Asked 10 Mar: due 7 Apr.
#ASSERT `s 22B -- must I be given a reasons statement` TRUE `2 Mar 2026` 0 TRUE `10 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `7 Apr 2026` `8 Apr 2026` EQUALS `REASONS IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 22B -- must I be given a reasons statement` TRUE `2 Mar 2026` 0 TRUE `10 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `8 Apr 2026` `8 Apr 2026` EQUALS `REASONS LATE`
#ASSERT `s 22B -- must I be given a reasons statement` TRUE `2 Mar 2026` 0 TRUE `10 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` `7 Apr 2026` EQUALS `REASONS NOT YET DUE`
#ASSERT `s 22B -- must I be given a reasons statement` TRUE `2 Mar 2026` 0 TRUE `10 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` `8 Apr 2026` EQUALS `REASONS LATE`
-- Asked on the last day (30 Mar): s 22B applies; asked the day after (31 Mar): it does not, unless the rules allow longer.
#ASSERT `s 22B -- must I be given a reasons statement` TRUE `2 Mar 2026` 0 TRUE `30 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` `1 Apr 2026` EQUALS `REASONS NOT YET DUE`
#ASSERT `s 22B -- must I be given a reasons statement` TRUE `2 Mar 2026` 0 TRUE `31 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` `1 Apr 2026` EQUALS `S22B NOT APPLY`
#ASSERT `s 22B -- must I be given a reasons statement` TRUE `2 Mar 2026` 42 TRUE `31 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` `1 Apr 2026` EQUALS `REASONS NOT YET DUE`
-- Not in writing; not reviewable.
#ASSERT `s 22B -- must I be given a reasons statement` TRUE `2 Mar 2026` 0 FALSE `10 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` `1 Apr 2026` EQUALS `S22B NOT APPLY`
#ASSERT `s 22B -- must I be given a reasons statement` FALSE `2 Mar 2026` 0 TRUE `10 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` `1 Apr 2026` EQUALS `S22B NOT APPLY`
-- The three "unless" limbs.
#ASSERT `s 22B -- must I be given a reasons statement` TRUE `2 Mar 2026` 0 TRUE `10 Mar 2026` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` `8 Apr 2026` EQUALS `IN THE DECISION`
#ASSERT `s 22B -- must I be given a reasons statement` TRUE `2 Mar 2026` 0 TRUE `10 Mar 2026` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` `8 Apr 2026` EQUALS `ALREADY GIVEN`
#ASSERT `s 22B -- must I be given a reasons statement` TRUE `2 Mar 2026` 0 TRUE `10 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` `8 Apr 2026` EQUALS `CERTIFICATE`
-- s 22D: declaration 15 Jun 2026 -> additional statement by 13 Jul 2026.
#ASSERT `s 22D -- the last day for the additional statement` `15 Jun 2026` EQUALS `13 Jul 2026`

§ `s 22T -- assistance`

#ASSERT `s 22T -- can I get legal or financial assistance` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `ASSISTANCE MAY`
#ASSERT `s 22T -- can I get legal or financial assistance` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `ASSISTANCE NO`
#ASSERT `s 22T -- can I get legal or financial assistance` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `ASSISTANCE NO`
#ASSERT `s 22T -- can I get legal or financial assistance` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `ASSISTANCE APPLY`
#ASSERT `s 22T -- can I get legal or financial assistance` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `ASSISTANCE NOT PART 4A`

§ `ss 48, 48A, 49 -- costs`

-- In my favour.
#ASSERT `ss 48, 48A, 49 -- what costs can the other party be ordered to pay me` `the applicant` `civil` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS (LIST `FEES`)
#ASSERT `ss 48, 48A, 49 -- what costs can the other party be ordered to pay me` `the applicant` `civil` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS (LIST `FEES`, `DELAY COSTS`, `BREACH COSTS`)
#ASSERT `ss 48, 48A, 49 -- what costs can the other party be ordered to pay me` `the applicant` `civil` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `ss 48, 48A, 49 -- what costs can the other party be ordered to pay me` `the respondent` `civil` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `ss 48, 48A, 49 -- what costs can the other party be ordered to pay me` `the respondent` `planning review` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS (LIST `PLANNING COSTS`)
#ASSERT `ss 48, 48A, 49 -- what costs can the other party be ordered to pay me` `the applicant` `planning review` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `ss 48, 48A, 49 -- what costs can the other party be ordered to pay me` `the applicant` `FOI review` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS (LIST `FEES`, `FOI COSTS`)
#ASSERT `ss 48, 48A, 49 -- what costs can the other party be ordered to pay me` `the applicant` `FOI review` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS EMPTY
-- Against me.
